            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "the neck-band or collar of a shirt, originally used to make it fit closely round the neck, afterwards expanded ornamentally. Hence, in 16^th and 17^th century, a collar or ruff worn round the neck by man or woman (OED s.v. band n.^2 4a), here made in Flanders | the neck-band or collar of a shirt, originally used to make it fit closely round the neck, afterwards expanded ornamentally. Hence, in 16th and 17th century, a collar or ruff worn round the neck by man or woman (OED s.v. band n.2 4a) | in medieval armor, a sallette is a light globular head-piece, either with or without a vizor, and without a crest, the lower part curving outwards behind (OED s.v. sallet, salade), but the meaning of bandes in this context is unknown" ;
